# OpenCode iOS port patch -- 0011
# Title: iPhoneOS: no interactive TUI (OpenTUI has no iOS renderer) -> actionable headless guidance
# Upstream: anomalyco/opencode @ e8238bae9b807b72ecfc75afd3a9fe2e6b07b944 (v2.2.5)
# Requires: patches 0001-0010 applied first.
# Files: packages/cli/src/util/ios.ts (new), packages/cli/src/commands/handlers/default.ts,
#        packages/cli/src/commands/handlers/mini.ts
# Why (device-reported): running plain `opencode` (or `opencode mini`) on the iPhone aborts inside
#      OpenTUI native renderer initialization with "Unsupported OpenTUI Node asset target: ios-arm64"
#      plus a native stack trace. OpenTUI ships no iPhoneOS renderer, so both TUI frontends cannot
#      start on this port; the headless CLI is the supported interface. This patch adds a shared
#      helper (isIOS(), TUI_UNAVAILABLE_MESSAGE, reportTUIUnavailable()) and checks it at the top of
#      the root TUI handler and the mini handler, BEFORE any background server start: the CLI prints
#      a user-friendly message (headless commands + docs path) to stderr and exits 1 with no stack
#      trace or "Starting background server..." noise. A defensive Effect.catchCause around the
#      renderer entry points degrades any future renderer-initialization failure to the same
#      message. Non-iOS behavior is unchanged (isIOS() is false).
# Test: artifact + stock host Node: `node opencode.mjs` and `node opencode.mjs mini` with
#       OPENCODE_IOS=1 print the guidance and exit 1; host smoke commands stay green; device PTY test.
# Status: iOS-only guard; TUI/PTY remains a documented limitation (§8/§12 of docs/OPENCODE_BUILD.md).

